WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960
Good to have you on the positive papers, the due positive podcast, Episode 8 for July 12,

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:10.940
2026. I'm Dan, and as always, Patrick's with me. The antidote to doom scrolling starts now.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.520
Morning! I spent last night reading the numbers on that new saliva test.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.720
The one that drops endometriosis diagnosis from nine years down today's?

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:27.300
Exactly. Two tests cleared for NHS rollout, endo-sure and endo-test. Both working off biomarkers in

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:33.440
spit. Nine years is a long time to live with uncertainty, and the mechanism is straightforward once you see it.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.220
saliva carries the same protein signals they use to hunt with invasive procedures.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.260
So patients get clarity fast enough to start treatment before things get worse.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:47.340
Time for the positive papers. Start with the endometriosis test. The approval covers

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:53.220
national use across the whole UK system. Researchers are seeing it game-changing because earlier

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:57.340
confirmation means treatment can begin while symptoms are still manageable.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.280
From an operation side, the big win is skipping repeated specialist visits and the weight

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:07.220
that used to stretch almost a decade. The saliva route also removes the need for surgical

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:11.300
confirmation in the first pass, which lowers risk and cost.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:16.860
Still early days on real-world accuracy across bigger populations, but the guidance just dropped this

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:22.160
month, so we will see the data soon. For the individual that shorter timeline is the part that matters

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:27.020
most. Next story feels like it came straight out of a lab that got tired of extra steps.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:32.560
The robotic system that sorts gram positive from gram negative bacteria by touch alone.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:36.880
No staining, no chemicals, no trained tech reading slides under a microscope.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:42.940
Traditional gram staining takes multiple manual steps and still leaves room for interpretation error.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:47.240
This robot collapses all of that into a physical measurement.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:51.300
Applications line up fast. Hospitals deciding on antibiotics quicker,

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.640
food plants checking contamination, environmental samples.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.520
The split into those two big groups is exactly what guides first treatment choices,

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:02.940
so the time-saved could matter in infection cases.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:07.780
It is still research phased though, so clinical validation and regulatory steps are ahead.

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:13.940
Fair, but the core idea removes the chemical and human bottlenecks that slow everything else down.

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:19.120
Last one jumps to launch sites. China recaptured a fish stage booster on Friday.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:24.400
Their first orbital-class reuse demonstration. They follow the landing profile space

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.900
X proved out and state media confirms the stage stayed intact.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:32.520
Lower marginal cost per flight is the obvious next step if they can repeat it.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:36.000
The test gives them data on structural margins and landing precision,

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:40.960
but repeated reuse cycles and payload performance under reuse are still open questions.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.940
It adds one more operator that can fly hardware more than once.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:49.700
I keep coming back to how fast the learning curve moves once you have actual flight data instead of

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:54.680
models. Space X daily reported booster 20's record duration static fire.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.760
The firing moves starship flight 13 to a July 15 target.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:03.740
The test specifically examines thermal margins needed for rapid booster reuse.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:09.080
Record duration on the ground run supplies fresh data on hardware limits under extended load.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:14.340
Flight 13, planning now, incorporates the performance figures from this static fire.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:20.000
Listeners following orbital reuse timelines will find the exact measurements in that coverage.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:23.000
Worth checking if you track the numbers on thermal performance.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:24.520
Think positive time.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:29.180
Mihali Chikcent Mihali described flow as the state where action and awareness merge,

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:31.820
especially when the task matches skill to challenge.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:38.160
The claim is that estructuring small daily actions around clear goals and quick feedback puts you in

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.120
that state more often and cuts down on rumination.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:45.480
The endometriosis test shows how removing a long weight restores forward motion.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:48.920
Same idea shows up in the robot and the rocket stories.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:52.620
Steady technical steps beat waiting for perfect conditions.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.480
The concrete rep is simple.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:58.920
Write the smallest action you can finish in the next 15 minutes and start it before you check

00:03:58.920 --> 00:03:59.360
messages.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:01.120
That brings us to the lever.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:06.460
Request a free or low cost home solar assessment from a local installer and compare two or three

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:08.980
quotes sized to your average electricity use.

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:13.200
Assessments take one to two hours and usually cost nothing upfront.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:18.520
Typical rooftop arrays in moderate climates cover 15 to 25 percent of household needs,

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:22.440
with payback in six to 10 years depending on local rates and incentives.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:27.860
One in 20 listener households completing an assessment and later installing would shift several

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:29.980
thousand homes off peak grid demand.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:35.260
The assessment itself answers the roof qualification question with site data before any commitment.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:38.240
The process starts with a call or online request

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:41.740
and ends with written quotes you can review on your own schedule.

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:46.460
Early results from similar programs suggest households that move from assessment to install

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:49.480
often see measurable build reductions inside the first year.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:54.720
I still wonder whether this is the single highest leverage hour for most listeners right now.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:58.620
The barrier the briefing names is not knowing whether the roof even qualifies

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:01.660
and the assessment removes that uncertainty with hard numbers.

